# Production hosts

Apex is `tszyin.com`. Apps are **subdomains of that host**. Jaxfr is **not** `jaxfr.*`.

| App (`SUBDOMAINS`) | Production | Local (default `ng serve`) |
|---|---|---|
| Jaxfr (`jaxfr`, default) | `https://app.tszyin.com` | `http://localhost:4200` |
| Filelink (`filelink`) | `https://filelink.tszyin.com` | hostname starting with `filelink` |
| Share (`share`) | `https://share.tszyin.com` | hostname starting with `share` |
| Time (`time`) | `https://time.tszyin.com` | hostname starting with `time` |

`getCurrentSubdomain()` returns Filelink / Share / Time only when `hostname.startsWith` that prefix; **everything else is Jaxfr** (including `app.tszyin.com` and `localhost`).

Password reset (`/reset-password`) lives on **Jaxfr only**. Do **not** use `{{ .ConfirmationURL }}` in the Reset Password email — that hits `/auth/v1/verify` and then Auth's **Site URL**. A leftover `http://localhost:3000` Site URL produces exactly that redirect (and scanners prefetching `/verify` burn the one-time token → `otp_expired`).

Email template button href (production):

`https://app.tszyin.com/reset-password?token_hash={{ .TokenHash }}&type=recovery`

Authentication → URL Configuration (still set these; Site URL is used elsewhere):

- **Site URL:** `https://app.tszyin.com` (not `http://localhost:3000`)
- **Redirect URLs:**
  - `http://localhost:4200/reset-password`
  - `https://app.tszyin.com/reset-password`

`send-password-reset` allowlist must match those two. Do not allowlist `jaxfr.` as if it were the production host. Share public URLs are `https://share.tszyin.com/<accessKey>/<moduleId>`.
